Adds the bilinear J_T form (jTbil), the inner integral of the generator
P₂ = gen 0 {2}, stratified integration for any stratum-dependent
integrand, single-coordinate Dirichlet weights (the exponent of the group
containing the coordinate rises by e), the placement of a distinguished
coordinate in R, K or neither, and the closed form of
J_T[P₂, 1] = (N+1) ∫_{T̂} (U² P̂₂ + U⁴/3) for every N ≥ 1 and admissible
data. At Table 3 a kernel certificate (266 piece lemmas) gives
J_T[P₂, 1] ≈ 4.99944 × 10⁻⁵⁷ as an explicit rational. Adds
Comparator/power_sum_entry_v2g.json, the certificate generator, controls,
the result record, and the roadmap with a calibrated cost model for the
full marginal Gram computation.

